A||||4||Dan87GT||Poly bushing install question||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||03-12-2000||07:01 AM||||I am ready to install my Prothane bushings into my engine cradle. I have two questions:    On the front of the cradle is the large OD of the bushing on the inboard or outboard side of the cradle??  Also on the rear of the cradle which half of the bushing is on top? - the half that fits in the frame??||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||03-12-2000||09:59 AM||||I just put them in my cradle and I put the large end in on the front and the large end up on the rear. I don't know if this is right or not but it looks right. And I got the cradle back in the car OK. Good Luck ||||reg||14
Z||000002||batboy||03-12-2000||12:57 PM||||Are you guys putting the poly bushings in without dropping the cradle? If so, how?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||03-12-2000||03:56 PM||||the bushings have number cast in. the one ending in 5 is the lower. it's the donut.<P>If you look at the existing front bushing sleave you'll see one end is bigger than the other. that should be the big end of the new poly.<P>Bat's on the 4 and V6 there's enough play to do the front then the rear. (Don't do the rear then the front. the poly doesn't have enough play & can bend things.) you only need drop about 2-3 inches. I don't know if the V8 has enough clearance. you might have to free all 4 craddle mounts at the same time so you can drop straight down. even then as long as you have a 2-3 inches slack in hoses and wires it should save a full disconnect.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||03-12-2000||11:16 PM||||I just did mine a couple of weeks ago and the  fronts only fit one way because it is larger on one side than the other.  The rear ones were pretty straight forward as well since they are fitted to the metal piece that goes between the cradle bushing and the frame.||||reg||1
